From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:02:45 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] lynx-pacing

Beetle Lynx reports a constant 75 fps, but each retro_run is one Lynx
display frame of whatever length the game programmed: 59.9 Hz as the
boot ROM leaves the timers, 75 Hz only for a game that sets it. Pacing
from the reported 75 would run most games 25% fast. For a core that
does not report its own rate (Core::reports_its_frame_rate, false only
for Beetle Lynx) the emu measures the rate from the sound each frame
carries, 20 frames at a time, and takes it once two windows in a row
agree within 0.5 fps and it moved more than 0.1 fps; a window outside
50 to 80 fps or a frame with no sound is ignored. The measured rate
then goes through the PAL pacing path unchanged: 59.9 Hz stays on the
panel tick, 75 Hz runs 1 or 2 frames a tick with all its sound. Until
the first measure the core is paced on the panel tick at its own
sample rate. Every other core never enters this code.

The Lynx Screen section gains Lynx Speed: Native (default) or Panel,
which runs one frame a tick (a 75 Hz game then plays at 80%), stored as
lynx in Config/pal_speed.txt. EmuHandle::paced_fps reports the period
in use. Measuring from the sound follows nelynes/slotPlus 0848fcb and
b264635 (GPL-3.0),
https://github.com/nelynes/slotPlus/commit/0848fcb
https://github.com/nelynes/slotPlus/commit/b264635
